CHASE LEMMA 2 (PROFILE / LP_exc^rel) — ADVERSARY REPORT

0. TARGET AND UPFRONT VERDICT

Target (notes/subthird_results.md:83, notes/hatch_results.md:131, src/grdeg/ledger.py:37):
Fix a base number field k of degree e = [k : Q] >= 2 with positive unit rank. Take linked fields K, K' of relative degree n over k (d = en, D = 2en) and a reduced linked O_k-module M = O_k w_1 + ... + O_k w_m subset O_K x O_{K'} of relative rank m (absolute rank r = em) whose unital reductions to Z/N agree on M. At the L[1/4] balance, x = log N, F_{1/4} = x^{1/4}(log x)^{3/4}, d ~ sqrt(x/log x), r ~ F_{1/4}, box Omega = [-1, 1]^r (|Omega| = 3^r), log B ~ F_{1/4}, and log Y ~ sqrt(x log x). Under conditional Dickman smoothness H and quota R (notes/lowerbound_results.md:32-47), beating L[1/3] via M requires N_ind(M, Omega; Y) * rho(log Y / log B) >= pi(B), where N_ind counts O_k^*-inequivalent candidates with 0 < |F| <= Y whose two-sided prime-ideal parity rows are independent modulo (a) proper k-subspaces and (b) products of lower-norm candidates.

Verdict: PARTIAL (adversary refutes unquotiented small-norm O_k^*-orbit scarcity at >= 2^m - 2 = exp(Theta(r)) orbits across m incomparable cones, proving both quotient clauses of LP_exc^rel are load-bearing; fails to refute full LP_exc^rel toward alpha < 1/3 because every full-support / non-subspace combination hits c >= 1; proves the Rank-3 Two-Hyperplane Relative Liouville Lemma and captures the 72-bit escaping witness). All scripts, pre-registrations, and extended proofs are in codex/scratch/ch_L2g/{prereg.txt,prereg_supp.txt,run_adversary.py,run_supplement.py,results.json,results_supp.json,details.txt}.


1. FOUR ADVERSARIAL CONSTRUCTIONS FOR GROWING (n, m)

Construction C1 — Pisot / single-seed relative units generalizing (s, s') (experiments/masullo_ext/mext_g/run_toy.py:266):
- Mechanism [proved]: Generalize the Q(cbrt(3)) norms-1-and-8 pair to arbitrary growing n by setting f(T) = T^n - c T^{n-1} + 1 and g(T) = T^n - (c - 1) T^{n-1} - b T^{n-2} + 1 over O_k, linked at small integer T = b coprime to N by choosing c in [1, bN] with b^{n-1} c == b^n + 1 (mod N) (pure modular inverse, no factoring of N). Note g(b) == f(b) == 0 (mod N) identically, while f(0) = g(0) = 1 makes both roots s in O_K^* and s' in O_{K'}^* exact relative units of norm +-1 despite generator height log c ~ x. One root s_1 ~ c is huge, while all n - 1 other conjugates s_2, ..., s_n ~ zeta_{n-1}^l c^{-1/(n-1)} have modulus < 1.
- Obstruction and ledger [proved]: Try to choose m >= 3 k-independent generators u_j = P_j(s) in O_K keeping |u_j(s_l)| = O(1) at l = 2..n and |u_j(s_1)| <= O(c) so linear combinations cancel at s_1. By Vandermonde / Cauchy inversion over the (n - 1)-cycle {s_2, ..., s_n} of radius c^{-1/(n-1)}, |P_j(s_l)| = O(1) forces the degree-k coefficient of P_j to satisfy |a_k| <= O(c^{k/(n-1)}). Any nonzero a_k in O_k with k >= 2 has |sigma(a_k)| >= 1 at some base place sigma, creating |a_k s_1^k| >= c^2 >> c at s_1. Scaling instead by negative powers s^{-k} merely shifts (c^{k/(n-1)})^{n-1} = c^k onto the product over l = 2..n. Thus only dim_k <= 2 elements stay at scale <= c; every full-support rank-m candidate pays |F| >= N^{e(m-1)} (log |F| ~ r x >> sqrt(x log x)), giving N_ind = 0 under Y and no sub-L[1/2] yield [heuristic].

Construction C2 — Multi-cone Lagrange relative-unit and small-norm seeds (codex/scratch/ch_L2g/run_adversary.py:298):
- Mechanism [proved]: Over k = Q(sqrt(2)) (e = 2), pick m distinct small integer nodes r_1, ..., r_m, set Q_m(T) = prod_{j=1}^m (T - r_j) and R_0(T) = 2T + 3 (so R_0(r_j)^2 - 2 takes small values -1, 7, 23, 47: an exact relative unit at r = -1 and small split primes at the rest). For b ~ N^{1/(n-m)} with gcd(Q_m(b), N) = 1, choose unique t in [0, |Q_m(b)|) so Q_m(b) divides A_0 - R_0(b) + tN in Z, expand the quotient in centered base b as monic A(T) of degree n - m, and set P = R_0 + Q_m A, Q = R_0 + Q_m (A + j(T - b)). Take the rank-m Lagrange basis w_j = (Q_m(T)/(T - r_j), Q_m(T)/(T - r_j)). Near each r_j, f = P^2 - 2 has a root at distance O(b^{-(n-m)}), placing the m seeds in m incomparable archimedean cones with |F(w_j)| = O(1)^m independent of N. Moreover, EVERY proper nonempty subset product w_S = prod_{j in S} (T - r_j) (1 <= |S| <= m - 1) has degree <= m - 1, hence lies in M with tiny norm |F(w_S)| = prod_{j in S} (R_0(r_j)^2 - 2)^2 = exp(O(m log m)).
- Exponent ledger [proved + heuristic]: Unquotiented small-norm O_k^*-orbits reach >= 2^m - 2 = exp((r/e) log 2) = L_N[1/4] (matching the 3^r box scale!). However:
  (i) Every subset orbit w_S is a multiplicative product of the m linear seeds (T - r_j), so over F_2 all >= 2^m - 2 two-sided parity rows lie in a subspace of dimension <= m = O(F_{1/4}) << pi(B) = exp(Theta(F_{1/4})) [proved].
  (ii) For ANY full-support candidate C_alpha(T) = sum_{j=1}^m alpha_j w_j (all alpha_j != 0), C_alpha(r_j) != 0 for all j, so Res_T(Q_m, C_alpha) != 0. Evaluating P^2 - 2 and Q^2 - 2 at the m - 1 roots of C_alpha hits A(T) of height b, jumping |F(alpha)| to ~ b^{4(m-1)} ~ N^{4(m-1)/(n-m)} (c = 1, restoring alpha >= 1/3) [heuristic].
- Toy measurement (T2, S2; codex/scratch/ch_L2g/results.json:85, results_supp.json:36) [measured]: Pre-registered on 48-bit split semiprimes at (n, m) = (6, 3) and (8, 4). At (8, 4) with E = 2, 29 distinct small-norm O_k^*-orbits appeared below 60^4 and spanned full k-rank 4 across incomparable cones, yet their exact two-sided ideal-parity rank collapsed to 4 (= m). Full-support small orbits: 0 in both runs; min full-support log|F|/log N was 1.660 at (6, 3) and 2.107 at (8, 4). This proves constructively that BOTH quotient clauses of LP_exc^rel (proper k-subspaces and lower-norm products) are load-bearing.

Construction C3 — Simultaneous multi-embedding cancellation via common-denominator divided differences (codex/scratch/ch_L2g/run_adversary.py:394, run_supplement.py:173):
- Mechanism [proved]: Generalizing cover.py's divided differences to force diffuse cancellation across almost all embeddings (evading C's few-embedding determinant bound, experiments/hatch/hatch_h2c/report.txt:20), set P(T) = D(T) A(T) and Q(T) = D(T) B(T) with D(T) = T^2 + 1 over k = Q(sqrt(2)). First, a syzygy trap uncovered in T3 (disclosed in codex/scratch/ch_L2g/prereg_supp.txt:3): on K = k[T]/(P - sqrt(2)), (s^2 + 1)A(s) = sqrt(2)*1, so [1, A, TA, ..., T^{m-2}A] has rank m - 1 once m >= 4. Replacing 1 by T^{m-1}A gives certified k-rank m (gens = [T^j A]_{j=0}^{m-1}, still containing sqrt(2)*1 = A + T^2 A). On K, theta(alpha) = sqrt(2) C_alpha(s) / (s^2 + 1) where C_alpha(T) = sum_{j=0}^{m-1} alpha_j T^j has pure O(1) coefficients! Consequently |L_i(alpha)| = O(mE) simultaneously at all 4(n - 2) roots away from +-i.
- Obstruction and ledger [proved + heuristic]: By Vieta and Jensen, for any full-support C_alpha in [-1, 1]^{2m}, its m - 1 roots xi_k satisfy prod_{sigma, k} |xi_{sigma, k}| >= (C_k E)^{-2(m-1)} and cluster near |xi| = 1, where |D(xi_k) A(xi_k) +- sqrt(2)| ~ b. Unless (T^2 + 1) divides C_alpha(T) — which happens even for full-coordinate vectors like (u_0, u_1, u_0, u_1) at m = 4, rotating theta(alpha) into the proper rank-(m - 2) k-subspace span_k(sqrt(2), sqrt(2)s, ..., sqrt(2)s^{m-3})! — |F(alpha)| scales as b^{4(m-1)} ~ N^{4(m-1)/(n-2)} (c = 1, alpha >= 1/3; N_ind = 0 under Y_agg).
- Toy measurement (T3, S3; codex/scratch/ch_L2g/results_supp.json:44) [measured]: With certified k-rank m, full-support points achieved |L_i(z)| <= 10 simultaneously on 16/24 embeddings at (6, 3) (60 bits) and 28/32 embeddings at (8, 4) (72 bits), yet full-support vectors under X_0 = 3^D 2^{ceil(bits/(2n))} were 0/729 and 0/6561 (min log_2|F| = 120.28 vs 43.04, and 63.57 vs 55.72).

Construction C4 — Abelian multiquadratic N-cancellation & CM unit-circle Side 1 (codex/scratch/ch_L2g/run_adversary.py:475, 577):
- Mechanism C4a (Factoring-free Kummer relative-unit tower) [proved]: Build K = k(s_1, ..., s_t) of relative degree n = 2^t (m = t + 1) with f_i(T) = T^2 - c_i T + 1, g_i(T) = T^2 - c'_i T + u_i linked at small b_i in {2, 3, 5, ...}. Since b_i c_i = a_i N + b_i^2 + 1 with a_i = -(b_i^2 + 1) N^{-1} mod b_i known without factoring N, c_i = (a_i/b_i) N + O(1) has a KNOWN rational multiple r_i = a_i/b_i of N! Choosing nonzero integers alpha_1, ..., alpha_t with sum_{i=1}^t alpha_i r_i = 0 cancels O(N) identically at all embeddings eps in {0, 1}^t where sum_{eps_i=1} alpha_i r_i = 0.
- Obstruction and ledger C4a [proved]: By Sperner's theorem (Littlewood-Offord), for s >= 2 nonzero terms, sum_{eps_i=1} alpha_i r_i = 0 holds on at most binom(s, floor(s/2)) / 2^s <= 1/2 of {0, 1}^t; the remaining >= n/2 embeddings keep |L_eps| ~ N, forcing |F| >= N^{en} = N^d (worse than L[1/2]). Meanwhile the 2^t = n small-norm monomials s^S span parity rank <= t = log_2 n << pi(B). Verified in T4 (results.json:145) [measured]: at t = 2 (alpha = [1, 2, -3]) and t = 3 (alpha = [1, 6, 9, -10]) on 48-bit N, exact arb certification showed 2/4 and 2/8 embeddings collapsed to O(1) while 2/4 and 6/8 stayed ~ N (log|F|/log N = 10.13 and 27.17).
- Mechanism & ledger C4b (CM / cyclotomic unit-circle Side 1) [proved + measured]: Take K = Q(sqrt(2), zeta_15) (n = 8, d = 16) with u_j = zeta_15^{j-1}: |sigma(u_j)| = 1 at ALL 16 embeddings, so H_1 = 0 and |W_1(z)| <= (r C_k)^d independent of N! Even granting an SNFS/oracle root Phi_15(b) == 0 (mod N) with minimal b ~ N^{1/8}, avoiding Type-A coincidence (notes/rankdegen_results.md:190) forces Side 2 g_rel(T) = Phi_15(T) + (T - b)(1 + sqrt(2)) (note Theorem KH unconditionally forbids H_1, H_2 = O(D) simultaneously, notes/subthird_results.md:27). Full-support C_alpha(T) of degree m - 1 then pays |W_2| ~ b^{2(m-1)} ~ N^{2(m-1)/8} (c = 1, alpha >= 1/3). In S4 at b = 600, 74 bits (results_supp.json:69) [measured], min full-support log|F|/log N matched 2(m - 1)/8 = 0.5000 and 0.7500 to four decimal places (0.4999 and 0.7499).


2. PRECISE RANK-3 TWO-HYPERPLANE RELATIVE LIOUVILLE LEMMA & 72-BIT WITNESS TEST

Why 1-hyperplane cover.py failed on the 72-bit witness [proved + measured]:
In experiments/masullo_ext/mext_c/cover.py:48, each single embedding L_i maps [-2, 2]^6 (15,625 vectors) into R^1 (for real roots) or C^1. At real roots, 1D Dirichlet pigeonhole packs 5^6 values into [-O(b), O(b)], collapsing single-embedding rank-3 thresholds to prod_{i=1}^{32} t_i = 2^{-68.1} << v_1 v_2 = 2^{48.29} < cap = 2^{55.72} (results.json:6). On z* = [-2, 1, -1, 1, -1, 0] (witness.json:1), sorted side-1 moduli begin [0.0104, 0.2298, 0.4571, ...] (results.json:9): |L_{i_1}(z*)| = 0.0104 exceeds the collapsed 1D threshold t_{i_1}, so z* escapes every W_i, yet z* is simultaneously small at TWO same-sigma embeddings (0.0104 * 0.2298 = 0.00239), i.e., near the codimension-2 point [L_{sigma, i} x L_{sigma, j}] in P^2! Furthermore, divided differences satisfy D(s) theta(alpha) = C_alpha(s) of degree 3, so full-support |F| scales as b^{12} ~ N^{3/4} (c > 1); z* only fell under cap = 3^32 * 32 at 72 bits (b = 22) because 3^32 = 2^{50.7} masked b^{12}, and full-support hits drop from 53 (72 bits) to 0 (96 bits, min log_2|F| = 120.52) and 0 (120 bits, 161.36) (results.json:61).

Rank-3 Two-Hyperplane Relative Liouville Lemma [proved] (full proof in codex/scratch/ch_L2g/details.txt:5):
Let k have degree e and Z-basis constant C_k = max_sigma sum_{t=1}^e |sigma(omega_t)|. Let M subset O_K x O_{K'} have relative rank m = 3 over k, with q = 2n relative linear forms L_{sigma, 1}, ..., L_{sigma, 2n} : C^3 -> C at each base embedding sigma : k -> C. Fix sigma_0 and 1 <= i < j <= 2n, and set
  tau*_{sigma_0; i, j} := ||L_{sigma_0, i} x L_{sigma_0, j}||_2 / ( 2 * 3^{(3e+1)/2} * (C_k E)^{3e - 2} ).
Then:
(i) For EVERY scale s > 0, the tube { a in [-E, E]^{3e} \ {0} : |L_{sigma_0, i}(a)| < s and |L_{sigma_0, j}(a)| < 2 tau*_{sigma_0; i, j} / s } spans k-dimension at most 2 (lies in a proper k-subspace W_{sigma_0; i, j, s} subsetneq k^3).
(ii) Since prod_sigma prod_{1 <= i < j <= 2n} |L_{sigma, i}(a) L_{sigma, j}(a)| = |F(a)|^{2n - 1}, every a in [-E, E]^{3e} \ {0} with |F(a)| < (prod_{sigma, i < j} tau*_{sigma; i, j})^{1/(2n - 1)} lies in the union of the D single-hyperplane subspaces W_{sigma, i} and O(e n^2 log(H + E)) dyadic rank-2 subspaces W_{sigma; i, j, s_k}.

Proof sketch: Form the 3x3 matrix B with rows L_{sigma_0, i}, L_{sigma_0, j}, and unit row u* = conj(v)/||v||_2 (v = L_{sigma_0, i} x L_{sigma_0, j}), so det(B) = ||v||_2. For three k-independent box columns A in M_{3x3}(O_k), prod_sigma |det(sigma(A))| >= 1. Row-Hadamard on B sigma_0(A) gives ||v||_2 |det(sigma_0(A))| < 9 C_k E s (2 tau*/s), and column-Hadamard at the e - 1 places sigma != sigma_0 gives |det(sigma(A))| <= 3^{3/2} (C_k E)^3; multiplying yields ||v||_2 < ||v||_2, contradiction.

Exact test on the 72-bit witness and all four cover.py fixtures (T1, S1; results.json:45, results_supp.json:2) [measured]:
1. Analytic bound check: Tested across all 240 same-sigma pairs and 25 dyadic scales (6,000 tubes) on the 72-bit divided-difference box [-2, 2]^6: 0/6,000 violations.
2. Parameter-free pair-prefix cover W^{(2)}_{sigma; i, j} (sorting box vectors by |L_{sigma, i}(z) L_{sigma, j}(z)| before dim_k = 3, zero tuning):
   - 72-bit divided: z* = [-2, 1, -1, 1, -1, 0] IS COVERED (both pair-product and balanced-max covers); uncovered unit classes drop 11 -> 6 (1 under 1h U 2h), and smooth incremental parity rank drops from 1 to 0 (15/15 smooth rank explained!).
   - 96-bit divided: 0 uncovered, 0 incremental rank.
   - 72-bit / 96-bit power controls: incremental rank drops 14 -> 6 (72-bit) and stays 3 (96-bit), because power generators (1, T, T^2) have tiny root modulus |zeta| ~ 1.5 (M_i ~ 2.5 < (C_k E)^2 at toy size) and b^8 = N^{1/2} < 3^32 * 64.

Scope for growing m [proved]: Generalizing two-hyperplane intersections to (m - 1)-hyperplane intersections at m ~ F_{1/4} incurs binom(2n, m - 1) = exp(Theta(m log(n/m))) >> 3^r tuples, so codimension-(m - 1) enumeration only works for fixed m (like m = 3). For growing m, KH gives average height H/D ~ x^{1/4}(log x)^{7/4}, which beats O_k(m) ~ x^{1/4}(log x)^{3/4} by log x, EXCEPT for Hadamard's (1/2) e m log m factor (~ x^{1/4}(log x)^{7/4}), matching C's growing-rank threshold obstacle (notes/hatch_results.md:132).


3. FINAL VERDICT AND NEXT STEP

Verdict: PARTIAL.
- Adversary side: No growing-(n, m) Type-D family achieved alpha < 1/3; all four mechanisms hit c >= 1 on genuinely full-rank, non-subspace candidates. However, C2 refutes naive unquotiented O_k^*-orbit bounds at >= 2^m - 2 orbits, proving that LP_exc^rel's proper-subspace and lower-norm-product quotients are indispensable.
- Prover side: The Rank-3 Two-Hyperplane Relative Liouville Lemma is proved and completely eliminates the 72-bit divided-difference witness's incremental rank (1 -> 0).
- What remains open: For growing m ~ x^{1/4}(log x)^{3/4}, removing the (1/2) log m Hadamard gap in C's threshold sum AND bounding the cumulative fresh parity rank contributed across proper k-subspaces under recursion.
- Concrete next step: Switch to the prover side on the subspace-recursion obligation — prove that any proper k-subspace W of dimension s < m contributing >= s + 1 multiplicatively independent smooth rows below Y must itself satisfy an induced ideal-relative KH floor T_W H_W >= x - O_k(D log D) with T_W ~ 4n/s (forcing s >= Omega(m) and terminating recursion in O(1) depth).
